From 0434635412c996b7a9129f6a5b6776323012aa68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:40:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/90] feat(netease): make the API gateway address
 configurable at runtime

Upstream reads VITE_NETEASE_API_BASE at build time, which is fine for a
self-hosted web build and useless for an APK that is already installed:
NetEase hands out playable URLs only to a signed-in account, so a web or
Android build needs an API instance, and there was no way to tell it which.

- providerApiBase: owns "which gateway applies to this provider" - the
  runtime override, the build-time value, and a describe helper that tells
  the four states apart (desktop built-in / set here / baked in / unset).
  Reads are synchronous because getApiBase runs before every request.
- Input is normalized (host-only input gets https, trailing slashes dropped);
  an unusable address is refused rather than written over a working one, and
  an empty box clears the override instead of storing an invalid value.
- Integration settings gains the field, with a Test button that makes a real
  search request - a format check cannot tell you whether the instance is up
  or whether it allows cross-origin calls.
- Registered in the command palette with en / zh-CN / in copy, per the
  settings-feature-integration contract.

The describe helper lives in providerApiBase rather than netease.ts because
omniArchitecture.test.ts forbids UI layers from importing provider internals.
